        "uuid": "512b708f_bbf48d7b",
        "filename": "java/androidmk.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 410,
      "author": {
        "id": 1962375
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-08T17:52:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe this split is necessary as I have seen some cases where `jniLib.partition` is not a single word, but comprised of multiple partition name with `/`, for instance `system/product`. In this case, `partitionTag` would be converted to `_SYSTEM/PRODUCT`, instead of the desired `_PRODUCT`. I am not totally certain if the last word in such sequence is always the module partition, but all of the cases that I have considered to be possible (ie `system/system_ext`, `system/vendor`) were the case.",
      "parentUuid": "dcc4c457_c078a95a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 410,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 410,
        "endChar": 51
      },
